[1mTests[22m ([38;5;10mtranslation/tests/[0m) load both [38;5;10mc_src/build/libStaticLoop.so[0m and the Rust [38;5;10mcdylib[0m via [38;5;10mlibloading[0m and call only exported symbols:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mt01_static_sum.rs[0m — ~20,500 lockstep comparisons of [38;5;10mstatic_sum[0m, including hand-picked boundary values, every power of two, a 20k-step xorshift sweep, and repeated [38;5;10mi32::MAX[0m/[38;5;10mi32::MIN[0m additions to force wraparound in both directions.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mt02_driver.rs[0m — [38;5;10mdriver[0m compared by capturing C [38;5;10mstdout[0m at the file-descriptor level ([38;5;10mdup2[0m + [38;5;10mfflush(NULL)[0m) and asserting byte equality, for strides −20..20 plus the boundary values, interleaved with [38;5;10mstatic_sum[0m updates so [38;5;10mdriver[0m is also exercised from arbitrary accumulator states.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mt03_symbols.rs[0m — asserts every symbol in [38;5;10mnm -D --defined-only[0m on the C [38;5;10m.so[0m is also exported by the Rust [38;5;10m.so[0m, and that each resolves via [38;5;10mdlsym[0m in both. Both export exactly [38;5;10mstatic_sum[0m and [38;5;10mdriver[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two things worth knowing about the design. [38;5;10mstatic_sum[0m owns a process-wide accumulator ([38;5;10mstatic int sum[0m in C, [38;5;10mAtomicI32[0m in Rust) that cannot be reset, so each library keeps an independent counter and all comparisons are done in lockstep — which is also why each test file holds exactly one [38;5;10m#[test][0m (cargo would otherwise run them concurrently and interleave the calls). And [38;5;10mcargo test[0m does not build [38;5;10mcdylib[0m artifacts, so the helper builds the release [38;5;10m.so[0m itself into a separate [38;5;10m--target-dir[0m to avoid contending on the outer build's lock; the tests therefore exercise the optimized library an external caller would link.[0m[0m
